  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Manohar Lal versus Commissioner of Police & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_3_358_392','2026INSC234'); ><font size='4'> <strong>MANOHAR LAL<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>COMMISSIONER OF POLICE & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 3 S.C.R. 358</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 234</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000812026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.K. MAHESHWARI<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Matter pertains to dismissal of police constable without conducting departmental inquiry, holding that it was not reasonably practicable to hold an inquiry. Headnotes&dagger; Constitution of India &ndash; Art.311(2) second proviso clause (b) &ndash; Dismissal, removal or in civil capacities under the Union or a State &ndash; Exercise of the power u/Art.311 &ndash; Registration of FIR against the appellant- constable posted in the Special Cell for the offence of robbery and thereafter arrested and taken in custody &ndash; While he was in custody the order of<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 12-03-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 13860/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_3_358_392','2026INSC234','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class